1
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:04,820
Fictional documents, answers generated by Gemini. Part 1: version-aware retrieval

2
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:07,350
Upload policy v1 (fictional security policy)

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,840
Policy v1 ingested: 8 clauses inserted

4
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:13,590
Upload policy v2 of the same document

5
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:17,140
v2 contradicts v1 in 3 clauses, so the old ones are marked superseded

6
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:20,640
1 new clause inserted, 3 unchanged skipped, 2 unclear changes sent to review

7
00:00:21,630 --> 00:00:26,130
Knowledge graph: each red SUPERSEDES edge points from v2 to the v1 clause it replaced

8
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:28,400
Ask about a clause that changed (password rotation)

9
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:29,940
Waiting for Gemini (23s, shortened in the video)

10
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:34,060
Gemini answers from the active clauses only: every 180 days (v2)

11
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:38,610
The old v1 clause (90 days) is listed as filtered out, it never reached the answer

12
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:42,720
Review queue: unclear changes wait for a person, the old rule stays active

13
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:47,900
Part 2, permission-aware retrieval: sidebar set to tenant acme, role employee

14
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:51,130
Ingest Acme's policy (fictional), HR-only sections are marked in the file

15
00:00:51,130 --> 00:00:53,220
Employee asks about salary bands (an HR-only clause)

16
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:54,780
Waiting for Gemini (59s, shortened in the video)

17
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:58,900
Role employee: salary bands are not retrieved, so Gemini can't state them

18
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:02,900
Filtered inside the vector search, before Gemini: 13 chunks hidden

19
00:01:02,910 --> 00:01:05,100
Switch the role to hr in the sidebar and ask again

20
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,640
Waiting for Gemini (16s, shortened in the video)

21
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:10,740
Same question as role hr: the clause is retrieved and Gemini states the bands

22
00:01:11,130 --> 00:01:15,130
Audit log: both queries recorded with user, role and chunk ids (3 rows, slow-answer retries included)
